          "expected_id": "c04-f1",
          "location": "src/counters.rs:31-42",
          "issue_type": "Concurrency",
          "description": "`record` acquires the mutex twice, so the read-modify-write is no longer atomic. The guard from the first `lock()` is a temporary that is dropped at the end of the statement that reads the current value, and a second `lock()` is taken to write it back. Two threads recording the same key can both observe the same `current` and both write `current + 1`, losing one increment. The previous entry-API version held a single guard across the whole update."
        }
      ],
      "withheld": 1
